& [RequestProfile] binds executable provider interaction identity
  + [profile_id] identifies one exact prompt schema and response compiler behavior
  + [current] is cantor-field-attention-requests/0.5
  + [historical] is 0.1 through 0.4 retained for evidence replay only
  = must: create a new profile before changing prompt schema output meaning or compiler behavior
  = must: store profile_id in every non-fixture report
  = must: verify a report with its declared historical builder and compiler

& [TypedProbeWire] is the profile 0.5 FIELD_ATTEND provider output
  + [candidate_member_ids] is a unique array of two through field-cardinality supplied IDs
  + [assessment] is coherent uncertain conflicted or excludes
  + [flagged_member_ids] is a unique array of supplied IDs and may be empty for a whole-proposal assessment
  = must: require flagged_member_ids empty when assessment is coherent
  = must: compile non-coherent empty attribution into one explicit whole-proposal finding
  = must: compile the wire into the base FieldProbe record before aggregation
  - never: let assessment itself mean validated rejected true or authorized

& [TypedDelineationWire] is the profile 0.5 DELINEATE provider output
  + [candidate_id] equals the exact provisional candidate ID
  + [status] is supported rejected or unresolved
  + [ordered_member_ids] is an exact permutation of all candidate IDs
  + [relation_kinds] contains exactly one fewer typed relation kinds than ordered IDs
  + [contradiction_member_ids] [excluded_member_ids] and [uncertain_member_ids] are unique candidate-ID arrays
  = must: compile exact self-bindings for every candidate ID
  = must: compile each adjacent ordered pair and corresponding model-selected kind into one directed relation
  = must: make compiler accounts identify the typed transform without claiming model-authored explanation
  = must: pass the compiled result through every base-specification delineation and latch gate

& [FaultReplay] preserves failed interface learning
  + [control_fault] has created field_validated faulted state prefix and zero or one control exchange
  + [probe_fault] has created field_validated probes_requested faulted state prefix and zero through four completed or failed probe exchanges
  + [delineation_fault] has the full candidate prefix through delineation_requested then faulted
  = must: recompute a response-backed fault from the exact sanitized provider response
  = must: bind completed exchanges to exact requests compiled proposals and stored records
  = must: reject altered fault text even when exchange digests are recomputed
  = may: validate the structure and preserved digest of a transport-only fault whose absent response cannot be recomputed

& [ControlBoundary] preserves an ordinary-pass comparison
  + exactly one control_probe_1 exchange compiles one FieldProbe
  + terminal state is control_completed
  + candidate delineation latch and fault records are absent
  = must: report latch status as absent and latch eligibility as false

& [AuthorityBoundary] remains unchanged from the base specification
  + typed compilation is an attention-local proposal interface
  + host admission is structural contract satisfaction only
  - never: claim truth semantic correctness permission hidden attention access generalized model reliability or production trust

& [SatisfactionSignature] binds this bounded amendment
